NGINX (pronounced "engine-x"):
===============================
NGNIX is developed by an Russian Developr Igor Sysoev.
Igor Sysoev originally wrote NGNIX to solve C10k problem.
NGNIX released as open source in 2004.
Today NGNIX and NGNIX PLUS can handle hundreds of thousands concurrent connections and powe more than 50% of busiest sites on the web.
It is a high-performance web server and reverse proxy server. In a typical React + Spring Boot application, NGINX can sit between the client and your backend/frontend and handle incoming HTTP/HTTPS requests.
A simple architecture is: 
User / Browser
                   |
                   | HTTP / HTTPS  
                   ↓
              +---------+
              |  NGINX  |
              +---------+
               /       \
              /         \
             ↓           ↓
       React Frontend   Spring Boot
       Static Files       Backend
                          |
                          ↓
                       MySQL

It is multifunctional tool. with NGNIX , user can use the same tool as a load balancer, reverse proxy, content cache and web server.
NGNIX supports micro-services to HTTP/2 protocols.
NGNIX is Docker friendly, which makes it first choice for Cloud based Applications load Balancer.
NGNIX supports N number of Open-Source third party libraries which makes it more flexible and expandable.
